{"version": "6.9", "hitCount": 10, "nextCursorMark": "AoIIPwvVoygxMjgwOTAwNQ==", "nextPageUrl": "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=TITLE%3A%22The+Cardiac+Insufficiency+Bisoprolol+Study+II%22&cursorMark=AoIIPwvVoygxMjgwOTAwNQ%3D%3D&resultType=core&pageSize=5&format=json", "request": {"queryString": "TITLE:\"The Cardiac Insufficiency Bisoprolol Study II\"", "resultType": "core", "cursorMark": "*", "pageSize": 5, "sort": "", "synonym": false}, "resultList": {"result": [{"id": "20354032", "source": "MED", "pmid": "20354032", "doi": "10.1093/eurjhf/hfq038", "title": "Improved survival with bisoprolol in patients with heart failure and renal impairment: an analysis of the cardiac insufficiency bisoprolol study II (CIBIS-II) trial.", "authorString": "Castagno D, Jhund PS, McMurray JJ, Lewsey JD, Erdmann E, Zannad F, Remme WJ, Lopez-Sendon JL, Lechat P, Follath F, Höglund C, Mareev V, Sadowski Z, Seabra-Gomes RJ, Dargie HJ.", "authorList": {"author": [{"fullName": "Castagno D", "lastName": "Castagno", "firstName": "Davide", "initials": "D", "authorId": {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0001-8491-152X"}, "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "Cardiology Unit, Department of Internal Medicine, University of Turin, Turin, Italy."}]}}, {"fullName": "Jhund PS", "lastName": "Jhund", "firstName": "Pardeep S", "initials": "PS", "authorId": {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0003-4306-5317"}}, {"fullName": "McMurray JJ", "lastName": "McMurray", "firstName": "John J V", "initials": "JJ", "authorId": {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-6317-3975"}}, {"fullName": "Lewsey JD", "lastName": "Lewsey", "firstName": "James D", "initials": "JD"}, {"fullName": "Erdmann E", "lastName": "Erdmann", "firstName": "Erland", "initials": "E"}, {"fullName": "Zannad F", "lastName": "Zannad", "firstName": "Faiez", "initials": "F"}, {"fullName": "Remme WJ", "lastName": "Remme", "firstName": "Willem J", "initials": "WJ"}, {"fullName": "Lopez-Sendon JL", "lastName": "Lopez-Sendon", "firstName": "José L", "initials": "JL"}, {"fullName": "Lechat P", "lastName": "Lechat", "firstName": "Philippe", "initials": "P"}, {"fullName": "Follath F", "lastName": "Follath", "firstName": "Ferenc", "initials": "F"}, {"fullName": "Höglund C", "lastName": "Höglund", "firstName": "Christer", "initials": "C"}, {"fullName": "Mareev V", "lastName": "Mareev", "firstName": "Viacheslav", "initials": "V", "authorId": {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-7285-2048"}}, {"fullName": "Sadowski Z", "lastName": "Sadowski", "firstName": "Zygmunt", "initials": "Z"}, {"fullName": "Seabra-Gomes RJ", "lastName": "Seabra-Gomes", "firstName": "Ricardo J", "initials": "RJ"}, {"fullName": "Dargie HJ", "lastName": "Dargie", "firstName": "Henry J", "initials": "HJ"}]}, "authorIdList": {"authorId": [{"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0001-8491-152X"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-6317-3975"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-7285-2048"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0003-4306-5317"}]}, "dataLinksTagsList": {"dataLinkstag": ["altmetrics", "wikipedia"]}, "journalInfo": {"issue": "6", "volume": "12", "journalIssueId": 1733347, "dateOfPublication": "2010 Jun", "monthOfPublication": 6, "yearOfPublication": 2010, "journal": {"medlineAbbreviation": "Eur J Heart Fail", "title": "European journal of heart failure", "essn": "1879-0844", "issn": "1388-9842", "isoabbreviation": "Eur J Heart Fail", "nlmid": "100887595"}, "printPublicationDate": "2010-06-01"}, "pubYear": "2010", "pageInfo": "607-616", "abstractText": "<h4>Aims</h4>Information on the effectiveness of beta-blockade in patients with heart failure (HF) and concomitant renal impairment is scarce and beta-blockers are underutilized in these patients.<h4>Methods and results</h4>The Cockcroft-Gault formula normalized for body surface-area was used to estimate renal function (eGFR(BSA)) in 2622 patients with HF, left ventricular ejection fraction < or =35%, New York Heart Association class III/IV and serum creatinine <300 micromol/L (3.4 mg/dL) in the second Cardiac Insufficiency Bisoprolol Study II. Patients were divided into four sub-groups according to baseline eGFR(BSA) (<45, 45-60, 60-75 and > or =75 mL/min per 1.73 m(2)). Cox proportional-hazards models adjusted for pre-specified confounders were used to assess the effect of bisoprolol and potential heterogeneity of effect across the eGFR(BSA) sub-groups. Older age, female-sex, diabetes and ischaemic-aetiology were more common in those with reduced eGFR(BSA). The hazard associated with bisoprolol use for all-cause mortality, the composite of all-cause mortality or HF-hospitalization and HF-hospitalization alone was consistently <1.0 across eGFR(BSA) categories with no treatment by renal-function interaction (P = 0.81, P = 0.66, P = 0.71, respectively). The rate of bisoprolol discontinuation was higher in patients with eGFR(BSA) < 45 mL/min per 1.73 m(2). Nevertheless the absolute benefit of bisoprolol was greater for patients with chronic kidney disease compared with those without.<h4>Conclusion</h4>The beneficial effects of bisoprolol on mortality and hospitalization for worsening heart-failure were not modified by baseline eGFR(BSA). Renal impairment should not prevent the use of bisoprolol in patients with HF.", "affiliation": "Cardiology Unit, Department of Internal Medicine, University of Turin, Turin, Italy.", "publicationStatus": "ppublish", "language": "eng", "pubModel": "Print-Electronic", "pubTypeList": {"pubType": ["Randomized Controlled Trial", "Journal Article"]}, "meshHeadingList": {"meshHeading": [{"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Humans"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Bisoprolol", "meshQualifierList": {"meshQualifier": [{"majorTopic_YN": "Y", "abbreviation": "TU", "qualifierName": "therapeutic use"}]}}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Adrenergic beta-Antagonists", "meshQualifierList": {"meshQualifier": [{"majorTopic_YN": "Y", "abbreviation": "TU", "qua